## Decision 10 - Blackbox

Problem: Slow or corrupt UTF-8 conversion must leave forensic evidence.  
Solution: 300-frame `BabelTelemetryEntry` ring records key, slice, per-frame translation count, active leases, conversion time, language, and flags; fault path writes `Dump_SHINOBU_39.bin` and `Dump_BABEL_SYSTEM.bin`.  
Rejected Alternatives: `Debug.Log` spam, managed List history, exception-only diagnostics.  
Scalability potential: Fixed memory on every tier; offline tooling can read the dump later.  
Hardware Impact: Estimated sub-2 us/event; dump path only on fault or >0.5 ms decode.

## Decision 11 - Async Binary Locale Swap Closure

Problem: Task 09 was still partial: the previous implementation deferred `SetLanguageAsync`, but did not read `.h8bin` bytes on a background thread or commit the DataVault pointer swap in `POST_SIMULATION`.  
Solution: Added a 32-byte aligned `BabelDictionaryStage` DTO, Vault-backed staging buffer `(BufferID)70543`, background MMF read with stream fallback, header/version/CRC/index validation, and `LocRegistry.TryCommitStagedBabelDictionary` called from `LocalizationManager` as an `IDispatcherSystem` in `DispatcherPhase.PostSimulation`. The active UTF-8 payload remains a Vault `NativeArray<byte>` and the typed language signal is fired after successful commit.  
Rejected Alternatives: `File.ReadAllBytes`, managed `byte[]` staging, `Task.Run` closure ownership, main-thread file I/O, direct mutation of string dictionaries from a worker thread, and adding a new contracts/asmdef dependency just to name a private Babel buffer ID.  
Scalability potential: Low uses the same background read and bounded payload copy while stripping rich text at decode; Middle keeps full authored text; High/Ultra can spend the freed main-thread stall budget on visual-only font/SDF treatment without changing gameplay truth.  
Hardware Impact: Main-thread MicroSD/SSD language-swap stalls are moved off-thread. Exact microseconds are not claimed; the shipped `Babel_Dictionary.h8bin` verifier reports 1,534,512 bytes, so the avoided stall is file-system dependent and still requires Unity profiler/GC proof.
